    "note": "Re-audited all direct build, runtime, optional development and Node dependencies against official registry candidates, including versions outside current bounds. The complete inventory and dependency manifest are unchanged from the reviewed 0.23.0 receipt; all latest candidates satisfy the existing declarations and Python 3.14, and all 15 installed Python direct packages match those candidates. No new upstream release requires additional release-note review. The change only makes interrupted source synchronization retries visible as one WARNING with bounded original failure context; source qualification, lease completion, publication, schema and configuration semantics remain unchanged. Targeted regression validation passed 126 cases, including a real stable invalid gallery with SQLite and unchanged source stat/hash across retries. Independent diagnostic robustness checks passed 14 cases. Explicit H2HDB_TEST_MARIADB=1 resident lifecycle validation against disposable MariaDB 10.11.11 passed one fresh-epoch source/analysis/publication case. The integration gate additionally runs bounded offline pytest, Lean, finite small TLC, distribution build and installed-wheel smoke. No dependency changes, migration or compatibility shim are introduced.",
